Religion, existence, and the meaning of life (@religion-existence-and-the-meaning-of-life: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_6HFHAD3C09XQ0Y1N0HMQ15414J
This material examines philosophical questions about religion, belief, reason, suffering, mortality, purpose, and ways of living. Compare arguments concerning religious claims and secular accounts of meaning, relating them to metaphysics, ethics, experience, and historical traditions. A route can begin with a text or existential question and trace its assumptions and objections. Keep the distinction between understanding an account, evaluating its arguments, and adopting it as a way of life explicit.

**Parent:** [Philosophy](../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).
